1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Vestigium: watch the sky move in real NASA SPHEREx pictures.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Real pictures, 2010 and 2026: Barnard's Star moved about 168″.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,000
We locked a Pluto forecast on GitHub
before opening the newest pictures.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
5.9″ off: 3,000× closer than a straight line, but
just outside our 95% oval. A published miss.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
We found why, and locked new forecasts for 2027.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Could SPHEREx see Planet X? We measured it: not in one image.
